#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:92
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pikemen,†1]]1. Pikemen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:103
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:142
msgid ""
"The pike is the traditional weapon of the mercenaries of Tilea. Twice as "
"long as a spear and even longer than a cavalryman’s lance this is a truly "
"fearsome although rather unwieldy weapon. Due to this Pikemen never benefit "
"from defended or fortified status when in dense terrain (even partially) or "
"on fortress walls etc. They still count as defended on higher ground or "
"behind low obstacles as usual.  Pikemen count as defended against cavalry or "
"chariots charging to their front, except when the Pikemen are in dense "
"terrain.  This bonus only applies in the first combat round of an engagement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:110
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Pikemen stands may only give or receive support by other infantry or Pikemen "
"stands that are facing the same direction and touching their flank with the "
"whole of their own flank. Any support behind or in front of Pikemen stand is "
"not allowed. In all other respects they count as infantry (movement/pursuit "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:113
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:152
msgid ""
"Pikemen are based as cavalry – i.e. the models are orientated towards the "
"narrow edge of the base."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regiments of Renown"
msgstr ""

#.  list, little, possibilities
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:10
msgid ""
"Regiments of Renown is an army list expansion designed to add a little extra "
"flavour and expand the possibilities of standard army lists. It presents "
"mercenary units that can be added (hired) to your existing armies. Their "
"rules are described on the following pages. Both players have to agree on "
"using Regiments of Renown before the battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Mercenaries are a common sight on the battlefields of the Warhammer world. "
"Not all of them are human, although most are. Amongst the Dogs of War, "
"freebooters from the frozen wastes of Norsca rub shoulders with Corsairs "
"from Araby and mysterious warrior monks from the east."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Sellswords are assured of ready and profitable employment.  The demand for "
"soldiery in the Warhammer world has led to the establishment of numerous "
"mercenary bands – soldiers who sold their services to whichever general "
"happened to require them. Although some generals are willing to hire "
"mercenary troops on a more or less permanent basis, most mercenaries are "
"hired only when needed. Besides, the fees charged by the very best fighters "
"are far too high for ordinary generals to pay on a long-term basis. The most "
"successful mercenary captains become rich and influential in their own "
"right, and their services are soon in demand throughout the Old World and "
"beyond."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:36
msgid ""
"There are many mercenaries around the Old World. They mostly recruit from "
"outlaws, pirates and renegades as well as simple adventurers looking for a "
"fight, wealth and fame. They gather in wandering bands, companies and even "
"entire armies around a charismatic and usually infamous leader and look for "
"an opportunity to fight... especialy to fight for a proper payment. They "
"call themselves – The Dogs of War."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:46
msgid ""
"Around them some are more recognisable than others, mostly by the name of "
"their leader. In the land of Tilea – traditional home of mercenaries – that "
"specific and the greatest formations are named Regiments of Renown. They are "
"the most skilled, acomplished and noble mercenaries affordable for the "
"wealthiest leaders such as kings, princes and mighty warlords.  Sometimes "
"they may be hired even by a Dogs of War leader, of course if he can pay "
"enough. In the restless Old World they usually have full hands of work to do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:53
msgid ""
"Mercenaries commonly form into itinerant bands under the leadership of a "
"charismatic or especially brutal leader. The most famous of these bands are, "
"more often than not, known by the name of their leader, such as Verthhold "
"Brekt’s Halberdiers, Hagar Whitefang’s Were-Marauders, Bradan Swiftleaf’s "
"Glade Riders, Khalag’s Sure Shots, and the renowned Golgfag’s Ogres."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regiments of Renown army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$regiments-of-renown.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Everywhere: RoR → Regiments of Renown
#.  a maximum of, each full, 1000 points of, Remove Additionally
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "For hire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:76
msgid ""
"Mercenary units are very popular in the Old World.  Each army list may add "
"(hire) a maximum of 1 Regiments of Renown unit for each full 1000 points of "
"army value following the Allies Table. Hired units count towards the maximum "
"allowance per 1000 points of the unit type indicated in the Hiring Regimens "
"of Renown section."
msgstr ""

#.  the extra point value is included in the
#.  remove therefore
#.  melee → combat
#.  or heroes
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Led by the Hero"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:88
msgid ""
"To represent the presence of a strong leader, Regiments of Renown units "
"including artillery and hero type cost 10 points more than their equivalents "
"in the other armies (the extra point value is included in Regiments of "
"Renown unit profile) and receive a +1 bonus to the combat Attack value of "
"one stand. Note that this gives +1 Attack in total, not +1 to each stand! "
"This extra attack is not included in the Army Selector profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:90
msgid "No magic item may be given to hired Regiments of Renown units or heroes"
msgstr ""

#.  humanised
#.  a lot → greatly
#.  stay independent → are unaffected by
#.  friendly spells
#.  unique listed unit
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Independent and Exclusive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:101
msgid ""
"Mercenaries recruit from many races and lands of the Old World. Living in "
"the Empire greatly ‘humanised’ them, but they still stay individual. "
"Therefore, they are unaffected by any army or racial special rules – neither "
"bonuses nor drawbacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:107
msgid ""
"Hired units can be ordered and brigaded without penalties, just like the "
"other units in your army. In case of a blunder make separate Blunder roll "
"for Regiments of Renown units if they are brigaded with other troops. That "
"means one roll for your armylist troops and one roll for Regiments of Renown "
"troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:111
msgid ""
"They cannot be targeted by friendly spellcaster’s spells and do not receive "
"any benefit from friendly spells and effects including area spells and "
"effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Additionally your army may contain only one of each unique listed unit. If "
"your opponent hired the same regiment, just roll a dice and decide who got "
"the ‘authentic’ one and who ‘impersonated’ one. Roll just for fun, without "
"impact in the further game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dense-terrain,†2]]2. Dense Terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:158
msgid ""
"Lumpin Croop’s Fighting Cocks are well used to sneaking about in woods and "
"bushes. No command penalty is applied to this unit on account of dense "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[throwing-weapons,†3]]3. Throwing weapons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:164
msgid ""
"The unit has a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this "
"unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and "
"shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still "
"needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[undead,†4]]4. Undead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:167
msgid ""
"The Cursed Company is undead, and as such the following rules apply to them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:170
msgid ""
"They never act on initiative. The unit only moves in the Command phase if "
"given orders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:173
msgid "They are unaffected by the −1 Command penalty for enemy within 20cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:176
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the −1 Combat penalty for fighting terrifying troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:179
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the Confusion rule – they cannot become confused for "
"any reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[repeating-crossbows,†5]]5. Repeating crossbows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:187
msgid ""
"Mengil Manhide’s Manflayers are equipped with repeating crossbows. They may "
"shoot once at ranges up to 30cm and twice at ranges up to 15cm. A unit of "
"three stands would therefore shoot 6 Attacks at a target within 15cm and 3 "
"Attacks at a target at greater ranges. They may shoot at enemies that charge "
"them – in which case they shoot 1 Attack per stand regardless of range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pistols,†6]]6. Pistols"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:194
msgid ""
"Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates carry pistols... loads of pistols! They have a "
"shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can draw "
"line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[ogres,†7]]7. Ogres"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:202
msgid ""
"Ogres flock to mercenaries for the chance of a good fight and as much as "
"they can eat. These creatures are notoriously fond of fresh human meat, "
"although they will eat practically anything that was once alive (or still "
"is). To represent this, if an Ogre unit can use its initiative to charge an "
"enemy unit of humans at the start of the Command phase then it must do so "
"(not Dwarfs, Elves etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[light-cavalry,†8]]8. Light Cavalry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:211
msgid ""
"Light cavalry formations have a great use among the mercenaries. They are "
"experts at outmaneuvering an enemy and harrying his flanks. Light cavalry "
"have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can "
"draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[birdmen,†9]]9. Birdmen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:220
msgid ""
"Only half-mad nutters like Tileans would try to fly! The Birdmen wear insane "
"contraptions of light wood covered in canvas that are shaped like wings and "
"allow them to glide on the air currents. These ‘wings’ allow the Birdmen to "
"fly and still use their crossbows as normal. Because they are awkward "
"flyers, they can be pursued by any type of enemy troops.  Birdmen are based "
"facing the long edge of the base in the same way as other infantry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[galloper-guns,†10]]10. Galloper Guns"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:225
msgid ""
"These are lighter artillery than Dwarf or Empire cannons; due to this they "
"are shorter ranged, but can make up for their lighter shot by producing a "
"higher volume of fire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:231
msgid ""
"Galloper Guns move 20cm. All the normal rules for artillery applies as well "
"as cannon’s rules for shooting (bounce through, no saves and reduction of "
"cover values). Because they are light guns they have a range of only 40cm. "
"They still may shoot at the charging enemy by firing ‘grapeshot’ as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragons,†11]]11. Dragons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:235
msgid ""
"Asarnil rides a Dragon. The Dragon can fly, increasing its rider’s move to "
"100cm. An extra [.edit]#+3/3# Attacks are added (included in Asarnil’s "
"profile)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:242
msgid ""
"The Dragon can breath fire if the character has joined a unit that isn’t "
"engaged in combat.  The fire breath has a range of 20cm and can be directed "
"against one target as for normal shooting with 3 Attacks that are worked out "
"in the usual way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:245
msgid "Additionaly Asarnil causes terror in his enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allies Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$regiments-of-renown-allies-table.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Available
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:257
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ⓐ"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:258
msgid ""
"Available for this army – see the <<hiring-regiments-of-renown>> section for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "·"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:259
msgid "Not available for this army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hiring Regiments of Renown"
msgstr ""

#.  In the whole section, p → points
#.  Additionally, dwarfs, "a bad idea"
#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:272
msgid ""
"Each Regiments of Renown unit counts towards the maximum allowance per 1000 "
"points of the unit type indicated in this section. Additionally there are "
"some restrictions in hiring specified units, i.e. Dwarfs would never fight "
"together with Greenskins or Elves, and hiring _The Cursed Company_ together "
"with _The Witch Hunters_ is a bad idea."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:274
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#.  chosen
#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:280
msgid ""
"_The player hiring the Alcatani fellowship in a Dwarf army may field up to "
"one Ranger unit instead of up to two in a 1000 point value army. Rangers are "
"highest point value limited infantry type unit in the Dwarf army._"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:283
msgid ""
"_The player hiring the Marksmen of Miragliano in a Chaos army does not "
"restrict any of his units._"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:287
msgid ""
"_The player hiring Braganza’s Besiegers in a Tomb Kings army may field up to "
"two monster types (chosen by the player)  instead of the three available in "
"the army list for every 1000 points._"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:293
msgid ""
"_The player hiring Voland’s Venators in a High Elf army may field up to two "
"Chariot units instead of three in a 1000 point value army or five chariots "
"instead of six in a 2000 point value army.  Chariots are the highest point "
"value limited units of cavalry or chariot type in the High Elf army._"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:297
msgid ""
"_The player hiring Asarnil the Dragonlord in a 1000 point Araby army can’t "
"field a Djinn monster mount as the limit is one per 1000 points. In 2000 "
"point army player may field one Djinn instead of two._"
msgstr ""

#.  Grammar singular/plurals improved
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pirazzo’s Lost Legion"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:304
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army. The Lost Legion cannot be hired "
"together with _Tichi-Huichi’s Raiders_."
